:: StoryTitle
Lab 2 - States, Variables, and Conditions


:: StoryData
{
  "ifid": "6029A629-0693-4A73-A7DC-31BCEB551755",
  "format": "Harlowe",
  "format-version": "3.3.9",
  "start": "Introduction",
  "tag-colors": {
    "Decision": "green",
    "Event": "red",
    "Outcome": "green",
    "Main-Event": "blue",
    "Endinbg": "red",
    "Ending": "red",
    "Start": "purple",
    "Done": "orange",
    "done": "yellow"
  },
  "zoom": 0.6
}


:: Attack [Outcome Done] {"position":"500,400","size":"100,100"}
You signal your squad to make an arrowhead formation with you at the front. With another hand movement the squad aims and shoots at the monster.

With the bullets piercing through its skin, the monster turns to look at the squad, charging at them.

Bullets fly towards the monster without making significant damage to it. The monster uses the claws on its hand to cause wounds on your team, catching Gamma-4-C with his huge hand and slaming him against the ground.

The monster lowers its head to bite the soldier head off.

Gamma-4-C: "Kill it! KILL IT!"

The rest of the team shoots to the same spot, hopping to distract the monster. But it isn't enough, the monster focused on the soldier.

You need to act fast.

[[Tackle the monster]]
[[Use a granade]]

(set: $firstChoice to "Attack")


:: Climb the tree [Main-Event Done] {"position":"1500,700","size":"100,100"}
You climb the tree (if:$wounded is true)[with difficulty, the pain is still there but you have enough adrenaline to keep going](else-if:$wounded is false)[with ease], reaching a high branch and observe your surroundings. You can see in the distance a bright light. Could that be the answer to close the portals?(if:$secondChoice is "Leave it agonizing")[
The whines coming from the monster are slowing down, it seems its close to its final breaths.]

You look around to find the best path to arrive there. You can see three posible safe paths:

The right path is between rocks that give cover but could be hidding something in between them.

To the left is the forest with tall trees giving shadow from the sun.

And foward towards the clearing zone. 

All paths lead to the bright light.

You climb down from the tree (if:$wounded is true)[carefully to not hurt yourself more and walk ]towards your group.(if:$reputation is "mid")[When you got close you heard them wispering.

Gamma-4-B: "I don't think we can trust his judgment, he was to fast to sacrifice one of us.

Gamma-4-D: "I'm not sure, maybe we could-"

They stop wispering when they see you close, just staring at you.]

What path will you take?

[[Go left]]
[[Go foward]]
[[Go right]] 



:: Command your team to shoot [Outcome Done] {"position":"1900,500","size":"100,100"}
You don't think that much of it and command the task force to shoot the deers, you know that this place is dangerous and can't risk it.

Your team shoots immediately and kills the deers.(if:$reputation is "mid")[

You hear one of your soldiers wisper.

Gamma-4-A: "Finally a good decision"]

There isn't anything left here, you can just keep going.

[[Keep going]] 


:: Destroy it [Outcome Done] {"position":"2300,800","size":"100,100"}
You grab a granade and throw it towards the machine, destroying it in the spot. A portal opens and you can see the base, the world behind you is collapsing more and more every second you stay there.

(if:$reputation is "high")[You guide your team across the portal, closing once the last one of them has crossed to the other side.

They cheer and scream, they survived because of your good decisions.](else-if:$reputation is "mid")[Your team quickly moves to the portal, crossing to the other side. Once everyone is out it closes.

The team mours the death of one of their own, the air feels heavy.](else-if:$reputation is "low")[The team rushes to the portal leaving you behind, you follow behind. The portal closing after you cross it.

The team looks at you with resentment, you know they will never forgive you.](if:$wounded is true)[
You walk away slowly to the base infirmary to get the wound treated correctly before giving your report.

Once you get medicine and a clean bandage you walk back to the team to meet with the superiors.]

Superior: "Follow us commander, its time you give us the mission report"

[[Follow]]


:: Flee [Outcome Done] {"position":"500,900","size":"100,100"}
You signal your squad to retreat back to the portal, the monster looks way too powerful to combat it.

You and your team slowly walk towards the portal, when suddenly you hear the snap of a branch close to you, you turn and see one of your teammates stepped on a broken branch.

Before you can think about anything else the monster sprints towards you all, attacking the closest person to it.

The monsters assault is overwhelming. In a last minute effort, you throw your knife aiming at the stomach, hitting the target and making the monster retreat.

The monster collapses, painful whines coming out of its mouth.

[[You stare at the monster]]

(set: $firstChoice to "Flee")
(set:$canInvestigate to true)


:: Follow [Ending Done] {"position":"2500,700","size":"100,100"}
You enter a room, sitting in one of the chairs in front of your superiors.

You: "Commander of the Gamma-4 task force here to give my report"

You grab a form that is in front of you:

Number of casualties: (if:$teamNumbers is "5")[0](else-if:$teamNumbers is "4")[1](else-if:$teamNumbers is "3")[2]

Final reputation: (if:$reputation is "high")[High](else-if:$reputation is "mid")[Mid](else-if:$reputation is "low")[Low]

Fond the secret button: (if:$hasClue is true)[Yes](else-if:$hasClue is false)[No]

Superior: "Good job commander, you can now rest"(if:$hasMachine is true)[

You: "Before i go, i have this"

You give them the machine, they immedietely recognize what it is.

Superior: "Excelent job, you will get a rise for bringing it back in one piece. You're dismissed.]

You leave the room, the mission being a success.


(text-colour:red)[''THE END'']



:: Go foward [Outcome Done] {"position":"1700,700","size":"100,100"}
You guide your group foward to the clearing, nothing can surprise you all there.(if:$reputation is "mid")[Your team is far behind you, looking at you with caution and distrust.]

You and your squad walk for a while, seeing the light closer and closer. (if:$wounded is true)[The adrenaline is slowly fading away and the pain increases, you know that there isn't that much time left before you can't keep going.]

[[Keep going]] 
(set: $thirdChoice to "Go middle")


:: Go inside the portal [Main-Event Done] {"position":"300,700","size":"100,100"}
You walk inside the portal, your team is not so far behind. The world before your eyes is full of blue plants, the sky color a nauseous green. This place makes you question everything you've learned about the universe.

You're taken away from your thoughts when one of your teammates points at a nearby clearing and talks.

Gamma-4-A: "Commander, monster ahead".

You turn around towards where the soldier is pointing. You see a monster roaming around, it is sniffing like it was looking for something.

You have 3 options. What will you do?

[[Attack]]
[[Hide]]
[[Flee]]


:: Go left [Outcome Done] {"position":"1700,400","size":"100,100"}
You guide your group to the forest.(if:$reputation is "mid")[Your team is far behind you, looking at you with caution and distrust.]

You see animal life, "normal" looking animals.

Your team spots some deer nearby. They're staring at your team, getting closer slowly, thats not a normal behaviour for wild deers and this dimension has proven you everything is hostile here.

[[Send one of your team to investigate them]]
[[Command your team to shoot]]

(set: $thirdChoice to "Go left")


:: Go right [Outcome Done] {"position":"1700,900","size":"100,100"}
You guide your group to the right between the rocks, the cover they give giving you all a sense of safety.(if:$reputation is "mid")[Your team is far behind you, looking at you with caution and distrust.]

In the middle of the travel you feel the land shake, you look up and see rocks falling in your direction.

You warn your squad and everyone hides behing a sturdy rock.

Once the rocks stop falling you continue towards the objective with your team.(if:$wounded is true)[The adrenaline from the near death helps you keep going.]

[[Keep going]] 
(set: $thirdChoice to "Go right")


:: Hide [Outcome Done] {"position":"500,700","size":"100,100"}
You look at the monster and decided it's too dangerous to fight it.

You signal your team to hide in some nearby bushes, waiting for the monster to eventually leave the zone.

The monster roams the clearing, sniffing, until it walks away and disappears toward some bushes.

You and your team relax, when suddenly one of the teammates is attacked in the back, being thrown a couple of meters towards the clearing. You hear a roar behind you, the monster attacked by surprise.

Your team shoots directly at the monster, dodging its attacks as best as they can.

You find an old wound on the monsters chest and charge towards it, grabing the knife on your belt and stabbing it directly on the old wound.

The monster whines in pain and retreats, collapsing in the grass agonizingly.

[[You stare at the monster]]

(set: $firstChoice to "Hide")
(set:$canInvestigate to true)


:: Introduction [Start Done] {"position":"100,700","size":"100,100"}
The world has changed. After the elite of the world experimented with multiverse, Exploration Portals have been showing up all over the world. Monsters that people had nightmares about now roaming freely in our land.

You've been chosen to command a task force named "Gamma-4", 5 strong individuals being part of it. Your objective is to explore inside these portals to find a way to stop this madness.

You and your team are equipped and ready to explore a nearby portal. 

The decisions you take will have consequences...

[[Go inside the portal]]

(set: $teamNumbers to "5")
(set: $wounded to false)
(set: $hasClue to false)
(set: $reputation to "high")


:: Investigate the monster [Outcome Done] {"position":"1300,500","size":"100,100"}
You are curious about that metal part, so with your knife you cut around it to extract it from the monster.

Once its out, you see that it is some sort of control with only 2 buttons: 'On' and 'Off'.

You put it in your belt, it might be useful later.

With the investigation done, you look back again at the tree.

[[Climb the tree]]

(set:$hasClue to true)


:: Keep going [Main-Event Done] {"position":"2100,700","size":"100,100"}
You finally reach the bright light, there is a machine there.

You know its the cause of all the portals. You need to stop it from creating them.(if:$reputation is "high")[
Gamma-4-A: "We will follow your command"

All the team is expecting you to give the order.](else-if:$reputation is "mid")[Gamma-4-A: "I hope you know what youre doing"

The rest of the team is looking at you with suspicion in their face](else-if:$reputation is "low")[
Gamma-4-A: "You better destroy it, or we will take action"

The rest of the team looks ready to kill you in the spot if you don't act right.]

(if:$hasClue is true)[You hear a beep coming from your belt, you look down and see the control making the sound.

An idea pops in your head, you can use it and maybe it will turn the machine off.

[[Use control]]]
[[Destroy it]] 


:: Kill it [Outcome Done] {"position":"1100,600","size":"100,100"}
Without thinking twice you approach the monster, using a knife you cut the monsters throat open in a single movement.

The monster whines in pain for a second before finally dying, its body collapsing completely.

Your team is treating the wounds and loading the weapons. Once everyone is back on their feet you look around, finding a tree tall enough to help you see around if you climb it.(if:$canInvestigate is true)[

You also noticed a metal piece attached to the monsters back. You can try investigate it.

[[Investigate the monster]]
](if:$canInvestigate is false)[You notice a metal piece attached to the monsters back, sadly that part was damaged with the granade.

][[Climb the tree]]

(set: $secondChoice to "Kill it")


:: Leave it agonizing [Outcome Done] {"position":"1100,800","size":"100,100"}
(if:$firstChoice is "Attack" and $attackDecision is "tackle")[You remember how close it was to killing one of your soldiers and decide to leave it to suffer, it doesn't deserve to have a fast death.](if:$firstChoice is "Attack" and $attackDecision is "granade")[You simply leave it there to agonize, your team isn't surprised anymore with your little care for others suffering.]

You look at your squad regrouping, treating their wounds and loading the weapons with ammo. Once everyone is back on their feet you look around, the monsters painful whines in the background, stopping when you see a tree tall enough to help you see around.

[[Climb the tree]] 

(set: $secondChoice to "Leave it agonizing")


:: Send one of your team to investigate them [Outcome Done] {"position":"1900,300","size":"100,100"}
(if:$reputation is "high")[You command Gamma-4-E to approach the deers, maybe they're just friendly after all.

Gamma-4-E approaches the deers with the hand extended towards them, the deer sniff the soldier hands.

Everything looks peaceful until one of the deers attacks the soldier, the antlers stabbing him and comming out trough his back.

The rest of the team shoots at the deers killing them. Running towards the soldier just to see him give one last breath.

The soldiers turn around and look at you with resentment, it was your order that killed him, you knew that this place isn't safe.

(set:$reputation to "mid")(set:$teamNumbers to "4")](else-if:$reputation is "mid")[You command Gamma-4-E to approach the deers, maybe they're just friendly after all.

Gamma-4-E: "I won't come close to those things"

You: "It's an order soldier"

With resignation the soldier walks slowly to the deers, theres something in them that scares him.

He couldn't even get that close before the deers attacked him, the antlers stabbing him and comming out trough his back.

The rest of the team shoots at the deers killing them. Running towards the soldier just to see him give one last breath.

Gamma-4-A: "I knew we can't trust you"

The team has little to none trust on you now.
(set:$reputation to "low")(set:$teamNumbers to "3")]

You just command the team to move on.

[[Keep going]] 


:: Tackle the monster [Outcome Done] {"position":"700,300","size":"100,100"}
Without thinking it twice you sprint and tackle the monster, succesfully moving it away from your teammate.

Because you acted so sudenly your team didn't cease fire in time. A bullet hits your thigh.

Your squad ceases fire and with the monster now under you, 2 soldiers run towards you and help keep the monster down, pulling a knife and stabbing the monster repeatedly in the chest area.

The monster pushes the 3 of you away but doesn't get up, staying in the ground agonizing and bleeding out.

The rest of the task force reunites and treats your wounds, you know you can't move fast anymore.

[[You stare at the monster]] 

(set:$attackDecision to "tackle")
(set: $wounded to true)
(set:$canInvestigate to true)


:: Use a granade [Outcome Done] {"position":"700,500","size":"100,100"}
You quickly grab a granade from your belt and throw it to the monster.

The granade lands right by your teammate side and explodes. A slight cloud of dust covers the area, your squad can't see trough it.

Once the dust clears you and your team see the monster in the floor with multiple wounds, whinning in pain and bleeding.

The soldier lays beside it, theres no clear sign of him being alive.

The rest of the squad stares at you, some of them with shock and doubt, some in disbelief you would act so recklessly.

You?

[[You stare at the monster]] 

(set:$attackDecision to "granade")
(set: $teamNumbers to "4")
(set: $reputation to "mid")
(set:$canInvestigate to false)


:: Use control [Outcome Done] {"position":"2300,600","size":"100,100"}
You grab the control and push the 'Off' button, the machine immediately shuts down and stops glowing, compressing itself into a tiny metal, you take it and bring it with you to give it to the superiors, one last portal opens directly to the base.

(if:$reputation is "high")[You guide your team across the portal, closing once the last one of them has crossed to the other side.

They cheer and scream, they survived because of your good decisions.](else-if:$reputation is "mid")[Your team quickly moves to the portal, crossing to the other side. Once everyone is out it closes.

The team mours the death of one of their own, the air feels heavy.](else-if:$reputation is "low")[The team rushes to the portal leaving you behind, you follow behind. The portal closing after you cross it.

The team looks at you with resentment, you know they will never forgive you.](if:$wounded is true)[
You walk away slowly to the base infirmary to get the wound treated correctly before giving your report.

Once you get medicine and a clean bandage you walk back to the team to meet with the superiors.]

Superior: "Follow us commander, its time you give us the mission report"

[[Follow]]
(set:$hasMachine to true)


:: You stare at the monster [Main-Event Done] {"position":"900,700","size":"100,100"}
The tension starts to fade away.(if:$wounded is true)[

You can feel the pain in your leg when you get up.

]The monster keeps whining in the background, slowly bleeding out. You are staring at it since the battle finished, thinking on what to do next.

(if:$firstChoice is "Attack" and $attackDecision is "granade")[Your team see you doubt, they're still in disbelief you sacrified one of your own to deal with the monster, they believe you will do that again if necesary, they now doubt you.](if:$firstChoice is "Attack" and $attackDecision is "tackle")[Gamma-4-C: "Thank you for saving me commander"

The soldier looks greatful towards you.](if:$firstChoice is "Hide")[Gamma-4-C: "I didn't tought the monsters could be this clever to surprise attack us"

The rest of the team nods, waiting for you to give the next commands.](if:$firstChoice is "Flee")[You walk towards the monster and retreat your knife, you know you will need it in the future.]

Would you end the monster suffering and kill it in an act of mercy, or leave it to agonize until it dies?

[[Kill it]]
[[Leave it agonizing]]
